---
title: Web Dev Setup
tableOfContents: true
---
The team uses [**VS Code**](https://code.visualstudio.com/) as the development IDE, & [**Node.js**](https://nodejs.org) as the JavaScript runtime environment.

The setup for all Web Dev repos are the same. Just ensure that you **pull the correct repo!**

---

## Prerequisites

You need to have [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/), [Node.js](https://nodejs.org), & [pnpm](https://pnpm.io/) already installed on your system.

## 1. Clone the Repo

### p3d-web

```
git clone https://github.com/p3d-project/p3d-web.git
```

```
cd p3d-web
```

### p3d-docs

```
git clone https://github.com/p3d-project/p3d-docs.git
```

```
cd p3d-docs
```

## 2 Install Dependencies

```
pnpm install
```

## 3. Run the site

### Build for development

```
pnpm run dev
```

You should keep an eye out on the terminal for your dev url. By default, it should be `http://localhost:4321` by default.

### Build for production

```
pnpm run build
```

You are now ready to code!
